## Dataset

**Source:** Kaggle — Messy Food Waste Prediction Dataset
**Link:** https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/messy-food-waste-prediction-dataset/data
**Size:** ~900 rows (train + test split)

**Description:**
A deliberately messy dataset designed to challenge data cleaning and preprocessing skills.
It simulates operational data from a food service environment, where the goal is to predict
the amount of food wasted (in kg) per day based on factors such as the number of meals served,
staff experience level, waste category, and date information.

**Key Columns:**
- `date` — date of the record (requires parsing and feature extraction)
- `meals_served` — number of meals served that day
- `staff_experience` — experience level of staff (categorical, contains missing values)
- `waste_category` — type/category of food waste (categorical)
- `food_waste_kg` — target variable, amount of food wasted in kilograms

**Challenges:**
- Missing values in categorical columns
- Outliers in numerical features
- Mixed data types requiring conversion
- Date column requiring decomposition into year, month, and day features
